<th id="A1.T2.5.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T2.5.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.4.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Intermediate piece-wise constant function class defined in (<a href="#S4.E7" title="Equation 7 ‣ Definition 4.5 (Piece-wise Constant Function Class). ‣ 4.1 Approximation for Hölder Class by Piece-wise Constant Function Class ‣ 4 Approximation Error Upper Bound for Hölder Class with Transformers ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>).</span></td></tr>
