<td id="A1.T2.5.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.5.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The Transformer function class with <math id="A1.T2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="D" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>D</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">D</annotation></semantics></math> blocks and shape layer <math id="A1.T2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S3.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ Transformer Architecture. ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>).</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.6.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:11.4pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="A1.T2.5.6.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> <math id="A1.T2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\&amp;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="1.110em">&amp;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\&amp;</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A1.T2.5.6.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="width:11.4pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></th>
<td id="A1.T2.5.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.6.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The cell width <math id="A1.T2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and the separation width <math id="A1.T2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> in Definition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition 4.4 (Quantization Grid and Cube). ‣ 4.1 Approximation for Hölder Class by Piece-wise Constant Function Class ‣ 4 Approximation Error Upper Bound for Hölder Class with Transformers ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a>.</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}~\&amp;~\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}^{p}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0.532em" rspace="0.532em">&amp;</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">,</mo><msup><mi mathsize="0.900em">δ</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">∗</mo></msup></mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">p</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}~\&amp;~\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}^{p}</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T2.5.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.7.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Quantization grid in Definition <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem4" title="Definition 4.4 (Quantization Grid and Cube). ‣ 4.1 Approximation for Hölder Class by Piece-wise Constant Function Class ‣ 4 Approximation Error Upper Bound for Hölder Class with Transformers ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.4</span></a> and its positional counterpart <math id="A1.T2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}^{p}=\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}+E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}^{p}=\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}+E</annotation></semantics></math> in Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 4.7 (Quantization Module 𝑓_{𝒯⁢1}). ‣ 4.2 Approximation for Piece-wise Constant Function Class by Standard Transformers ‣ 4 Approximation Error Upper Bound for Hölder Class with Transformers ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a>.</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.8.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:17.1pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\rm app}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>app</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\rm app}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="A1.T2.5.8.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> <math id="A1.T2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\&amp;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="1.110em">&amp;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\&amp;</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A1.T2.5.8.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_left ltx_inline-block" style="width:17.1pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\rm app}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>app</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\rm app}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></th>
<td id="A1.T2.5.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.8.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The approximation error <math id="A1.T2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\rm app}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>app</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\rm app}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#S3.E5" title="Equation 5 ‣ Problem Setting. ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>) and the best approximator <math id="A1.T2.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\rm app}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>app</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\rm app}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#A4.E56" title="Equation 56 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ D.1 Error Decomposition of Excess Risk ‣ Appendix D Details of Applications in the Regression Task ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">56</span></a>).</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.9.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:17.1pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\rm sta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>sta</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\rm sta}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="A1.T2.5.9.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> <math id="A1.T2.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\&amp;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="1.110em">&amp;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\&amp;</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A1.T2.5.9.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_left ltx_inline-block" style="width:17.1pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></th>
<td id="A1.T2.5.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.9.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The statistical error <math id="A1.T2.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{E}_{\rm sta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℰ</mi><mi>sta</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{E}_{\rm sta}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#S6.E14" title="Equation 14 ‣ Regression Tasks. ‣ 6 Applications in a General Regression Task ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a>) and the best empirical estimator <math id="A1.T2.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{f}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{f}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S6.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Regression Tasks. ‣ 6 Applications in a General Regression Task ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>).</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.10.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:17.1pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m28" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="A1.T2.5.10.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> <math id="A1.T2.m29" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\&amp;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="1.110em">&amp;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\&amp;</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A1.T2.5.10.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_left ltx_inline-block" style="width:17.1pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m30" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{s(\tau)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{s(\tau)}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></th>
<td id="A1.T2.5.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.10.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The optimization error <math id="A1.T2.m31" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tau" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>τ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tau</annotation></semantics></math> endowed by the solver <math id="A1.T2.m32" class="ltx_Math" alttext="s(\tau)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>τ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">s(\tau)</annotation></semantics></math> and the best numerical solution in (<a href="#S6.E11" title="Equation 11 ‣ Regression Tasks. ‣ 6 Applications in a General Regression Task ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>).</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.11" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.11.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:8.5pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m33" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>l</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="A1.T2.5.11.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> <math id="A1.T2.m34" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\&amp;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="1.110em">&amp;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\&amp;</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A1.T2.5.11.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="width:8.5pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m35" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math></span> <math id="A1.T2.m36" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\&amp;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="1.110em">&amp;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\&amp;</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A1.T2.5.11.1.2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="width:8.5pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m37" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></th>
<td id="A1.T2.5.11.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.11.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The square loss function <math id="A1.T2.m38" class="ltx_Math" alttext="l(x,y)=(x-y)^{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>l</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">l(x,y)=(x-y)^{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, the empirical loss <math id="A1.T2.m39" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\widehat{\mathcal{L}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">^</mo></mover><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\widehat{\mathcal{L}}</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S6.E10" title="Equation 10 ‣ Regression Tasks. ‣ 6 Applications in a General Regression Task ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>) and the population risk <math id="A1.T2.m40" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{L}</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.12" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.12.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:11.4pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m41" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="A1.T2.5.12.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> <math id="A1.T2.m42" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\&amp;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="1.110em">&amp;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\&amp;</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A1.T2.5.12.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="width:11.4pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m43" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></th>
<td id="A1.T2.5.12.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.12.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The covering radius <math id="A1.T2.m44" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mu" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>μ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mu</annotation></semantics></math> in (<a href="#S6.E15" title="Equation 15 ‣ Theorem 6.1 (Upper Bound of Statistical Error). ‣ Regression Tasks. ‣ 6 Applications in a General Regression Task ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a>) and the sample size <math id="A1.T2.m45" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.13" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.13.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m46" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\lesssim~\&amp;~\gtrsim" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0.032em">≲</mo><mo rspace="0.032em">&amp;</mo><mo mathsize="0.900em">≳</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lesssim~\&amp;~\gtrsim</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T2.5.13.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m47" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\lesssim B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≲</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\lesssim B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T2.5.13.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> and <math id="A1.T2.m48" class="ltx_Math" alttext="B\gtrsim A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>B</mi><mo>≳</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">B\gtrsim A</annotation></semantics></math> denote <math id="A1.T2.m49" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\leq cB" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>A</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>B</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\leq cB</annotation></semantics></math> for some absolute constant <math id="A1.T2.m50" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.14" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.14.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m51" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\asymp" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="0.900em">≍</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\asymp</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T2.5.14.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m52" class="ltx_Math" alttext="A\asymp B" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi mathsize="0.900em">A</mi><mo mathsize="0.900em">≍</mo><mi mathsize="0.900em">B</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">A\asymp B</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T2.5.14.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> means <math id="A1.T2.m53" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}A\leq B\leq c_{2}A" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>A</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}A\leq B\leq c_{2}A</annotation></semantics></math> for some absolute constants <math id="A1.T2.m54" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1},c_{2}&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1},c_{2}&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.15" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.15.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m55" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\cdot)~\&amp;~\tilde{\mathcal{O}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒪</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em" rspace="0.254em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.532em">&amp;</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒪</mi><mo>~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\cdot)~\&amp;~\tilde{\mathcal{O}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T2.5.15.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m56" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{O}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" mathsize="0.900em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{O}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math><span id="A1.T2.5.15.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> is used to hide constant factors, while <math id="A1.T2.m57" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\tilde{\mathcal{O}}(\cdot)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo mathsize="1.110em">~</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\tilde{\mathcal{O}}(\cdot)</annotation></semantics></math>ignores logarithmic factors.</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.16" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.16.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.16.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="font-size:90%;width:19.9pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m58" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathds{1}_{d}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathds{1}_{d}</annotation></semantics></math></span><span id="A1.T2.5.16.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;"> <math id="A1.T2.m59" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\&amp;" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo mathsize="1.110em">&amp;</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\&amp;</annotation></semantics></math> <span id="A1.T2.5.16.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_align_center ltx_inline-block" style="width:19.9pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m60" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathds{1}_{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathds{1}_{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math></span></span></th>
<td id="A1.T2.5.16.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.16.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The <math id="A1.T2.m61" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>d</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d</annotation></semantics></math>-dimensional vector and the <math id="A1.T2.m62" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d\times L" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d\times L</annotation></semantics></math> matrix with all one entries.</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T2.5.17" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="A1.T2.5.17.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><math id="A1.T2.m63" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{VCdim}(\mathcal{F})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext mathsize="0.900em">VCdim</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic" mathsize="0.900em">ℱ</mi><mo maxsize="0.900em" minsize="0.900em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{VCdim}(\mathcal{F})</annotation></semantics></math></th>
<td id="A1.T2.5.17.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb" style="padding-top:1.4pt;padding-bottom:1.4pt;"><span id="A1.T2.5.17.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">VC-dimension of the function class <math id="A1.T2.m64" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℱ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, see Definition <a href="#S5.Thmtheorem1" title="Definition 5.1 (VC-dimension). ‣ 5 Approximation Lower Bound with VC-dimension ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5.1</span></a>.</span></td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Technical Remarks</h3>

<section id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Reshape and Flatten Layers.</h5>

<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In Definition <a href="#S3.Thmtheorem2" title="Definition 3.2 (Reshape and Flatten Layers). ‣ Transformer Architecture. ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3.2</span></a> and (<a href="#S3.E4" title="Equation 4 ‣ Transformer Architecture. ‣ 3 Preliminaries ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>), we introduced the reshape layer and its reverse. We now provide an example of such layers transforming representations between vector form and sequence form.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Example</span> (Column Reshape). Suppose <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0},d,L\in\mathbb{N}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>L</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0},d,L\in\mathbb{N}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}=dL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}=dL</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{e_{k}\}_{k=1}^{d_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{e_{k}\}_{k=1}^{d_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> be the standard basis vectors of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e_{k}</annotation></semantics></math> has a <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> at entry <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> elsewhere). Let <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\{E_{ij}\}_{i=1,j=1}^{i=d,j=L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\{E_{ij}\}_{i=1,j=1}^{i=d,j=L}</annotation></semantics></math> be the canonical basis matrices of <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> (where <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E_{ij}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E_{ij}</annotation></semantics></math> has a <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>1</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1</annotation></semantics></math> at entry <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(i,j)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(i,j)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn>0</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">0</annotation></semantics></math> elsewhere). The following constructed <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R:\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R:\mathbb{R}^{d_{0}}\to\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> can be a reshape layer</p>
<table id="A1.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(e_{k})=E_{i(k),j(k)},~\text{where}~i(k)=((k-1)~\text{mod}~d)+1,~\text{and}~j(k)=\lfloor\frac{k-1}{d}\rfloor+1." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>where</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mtext>mod</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>and</mtext><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(e_{k})=E_{i(k),j(k)},~\text{where}~i(k)=((k-1)~\text{mod}~d)+1,~\text{and}~j(k)=\lfloor\frac{k-1}{d}\rfloor+1.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and its reverse <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{-1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{-1}</annotation></semantics></math> is defined as <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{-1}(E_{ij})=e_{(j-1)d+i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{-1}(E_{ij})=e_{(j-1)d+i}</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, for a general vector <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x=\sum_{k=1}^{d_{0}}x_{k}e_{k}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x=\sum_{k=1}^{d_{0}}x_{k}e_{k}</annotation></semantics></math>, the output of reshape layer (<a href="#A1.E17" title="Equation 17 ‣ Reshape and Flatten Layers. ‣ A.2 Technical Remarks ‣ Appendix A Additional Technical Notes ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">17</span></a>) is <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(x)=\sum_{k=1}^{d_{0}}x_{k}E_{i(k),j(k)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x)=\sum_{k=1}^{d_{0}}x_{k}E_{i(k),j(k)}</annotation></semantics></math>. For a matrix <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{R}^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math>, <math id="A1.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R^{-1}(X)=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{L}X_{ij}\cdot e_{(j-1)d+i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>d</mi></msubsup><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>L</mi></msubsup><msub><mi>X</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>e</mi><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>d</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R^{-1}(X)=\sum_{i=1}^{d}\sum_{j=1}^{L}X_{ij}\cdot e_{(j-1)d+i}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Approximation Error Upper Bound</h2>

<section id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h5 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Roadmap.</h5>

<div id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS0.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we derive the error upper bound for the proposed Transformer architecture on the Hölder class, followed by an extended discussion on the underlying theoretical assumptions.</p>
<ul id="A2.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A2.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Regularity Analysis</span> (Section <a href="#A2.SS1" title="B.1 Regularity of the Hölder Class ‣ Appendix B Approximation Error Upper Bound ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.1</span></a> &amp; <a href="#A2.SS2" title="B.2 Approximation Error Between Hölder Class and Piece-wise Constant Function Class ‣ Appendix B Approximation Error Upper Bound ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.2</span></a>): Establishes the regularity properties of the Hölder class, which facilitates the reduction to piecewise constant function approximation in the sequence form.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Module Construction</span> (Section <a href="#A2.SS3" title="B.3 Approximation for Piece-wise Constant Function Class by Standard Transformers ‣ Appendix B Approximation Error Upper Bound ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.3</span></a>): Constructs the three core Transformer modules.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Main Result</span> (Section <a href="#A2.SS4" title="B.4 Verification for the Approximation Error Upper Bound ‣ Appendix B Approximation Error Upper Bound ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.4</span></a>): Combines the above results to derive the final approximation error upper bound.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A2.I1.i4" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A2.I1.i4.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.I1.i4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Extended Discussions</span> (Section <a href="#A2.SS5" title="B.5 Further Discussions: Assumptions, Implications, and Practical Architectures ‣ Appendix B Approximation Error Upper Bound ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">B.5</span></a>): Justifies the theoretical simplifications while exploring the implications for real-world models.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Regularity of the Hölder Class</h3>

<div id="A2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The Hölder class has the following smoothness property.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_lemma">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma B.1</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Smoothness Property of Hölder Class)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x},d_{y},K\in\mathbb{N}_{+},\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>⊆</mo><msup><mi>ℝ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x},d_{y},K\in\mathbb{N}_{+},\mathcal{X}\subseteq\mathbb{R}^{d_{x}}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>, for any Hölder function <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="{f}\in\mathcal{H}^{\alpha}_{d_{x},d_{y}}(\mathcal{X},K)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">{f}\in\mathcal{H}^{\alpha}_{d_{x},d_{y}}(\mathcal{X},K)</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x,y\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x,y\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E18" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E18.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|{f}({x})-{f}({y})\right\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{d_{y}}K\left\|{x}-{y}\right\|_{2}^{\alpha}\coloneq c_{d_{y},K}\left\lVert x-y\right\rVert_{2}^{\alpha}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≔</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|{f}({x})-{f}({y})\right\|_{2}\leq\sqrt{d_{y}}K\left\|{x}-{y}\right\|_{2}^{\alpha}\coloneq c_{d_{y},K}\left\lVert x-y\right\rVert_{2}^{\alpha}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(18)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof:</h6>
<div id="A2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Without loss of generality, we take the component <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{1}</annotation></semantics></math> of <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f=(f_{1},\ldots,f_{d_{y}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f=(f_{1},\ldots,f_{d_{y}})</annotation></semantics></math> for instance. In the case of <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r=0</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha=\alpha_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha=\alpha_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Then since</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left|f_{1}(x)-f_{1}(y)\right|\leq K\cdot\left\lVert x-y\right\rVert_{2}^{\alpha_{0}},~\mathrm{for~any~}x,y\in\mathcal{X}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.497em">,</mo><mrow><mi>for</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>any</mi><mo lspace="0.330em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>x</mi></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left|f_{1}(x)-f_{1}(y)\right|\leq K\cdot\left\lVert x-y\right\rVert_{2}^{\alpha_{0}},~\mathrm{for~any~}x,y\in\mathcal{X},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS1.p2.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS1.p2.2.1" class="ltx_text">we can get <math id="A2.SS1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert f(x)-f(y)\right\rVert_{2}\leq\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d_{y}}\left|f_{i}(x)-f_{i}(y)\right|^{2}\right)^{1/2}\leq\sqrt{d_{y}}K\left\|x-y\right\|_{2}^{\alpha_{0}}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msubsup><msup><mrow><mo>|</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>|</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>α</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert f(x)-f(y)\right\rVert_{2}\leq\left(\sum_{i=1}^{d_{y}}\left|f_{i}(x)-f_{i}(y)\right|^{2}\right)^{1/2}\leq\sqrt{d_{y}}K\left\|x-y\right\|_{2}^{\alpha_{0}}.</annotation></semantics></math>
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS1.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">With equivalent transformations between the vector norm <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\cdot\right\rVert_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\cdot\right\rVert_{2}</annotation></semantics></math> and matrix norm <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\cdot\right\rVert_{F}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\cdot\right\rVert_{F}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain following corollary for the reshaped Hölder class <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}\in\bar{\mathcal{H}}_{d,L}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}\in\bar{\mathcal{H}}_{d,L}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#S4.E6" title="Equation 6 ‣ 4.1 Approximation for Hölder Class by Piece-wise Constant Function Class ‣ 4 Approximation Error Upper Bound for Hölder Class with Transformers ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>) when <math id="A2.SS1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x}=d_{y}=d_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x}=d_{y}=d_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_corollary">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Corollary B.2</span></span><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Regularity of Reshaped Hölder Class)<span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Suppose <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d,L,d_{0}=dL\in\mathbb{N}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d,L,d_{0}=dL\in\mathbb{N}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1]</annotation></semantics></math>. For any two sequences <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y\in\bar{\mathcal{X}}=[0,1]^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo>∈</mo><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y\in\bar{\mathcal{X}}=[0,1]^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> and any reshaped Hölder function <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}\in\bar{\mathcal{H}}_{d,L}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}\in\bar{\mathcal{H}}_{d,L}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{H}_{d_{0}}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{H}_{d_{0}}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\bar{f}({X})-\bar{f}({Y})\right\|_{2}\leq c_{d_{0},K}\left\|{X}-{Y}\right\|_{F}^{\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\bar{f}({X})-\bar{f}({Y})\right\|_{2}\leq c_{d_{0},K}\left\|{X}-{Y}\right\|_{F}^{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="A2.Thmtheorem2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{d_{0},K}=\sqrt{d_{0}}K." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{d_{0},K}=\sqrt{d_{0}}K.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Approximation Error Between Hölder Class and Piece-wise Constant Function Class</h3>

<div id="A2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma 4.6 (Approximation Error between ℋ̄_{𝑑,𝐿}^𝛼 and ℋ(𝛿)). ‣ 4.1 Approximation for Hölder Class by Piece-wise Constant Function Class ‣ 4 Approximation Error Upper Bound for Hölder Class with Transformers ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a></span> (Approximation Error between <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{\mathcal{H}}_{d,L}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{\mathcal{H}}_{d,L}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{H}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{H}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math>; Restatement)<span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span> <span id="A2.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha\in(0,1],d_{0}\in\mathbb{N}_{+}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>ℕ</mi><mo>+</mo></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha\in(0,1],d_{0}\in\mathbb{N}_{+}</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}=dL&gt;2\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}=dL&gt;2\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>. For any given <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> and a target function <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}\in\bar{\mathcal{H}}_{d,L}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}\in\bar{\mathcal{H}}_{d,L}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists an <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\delta}\in\mathcal{H}(\delta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\delta}\in\mathcal{H}(\delta)</annotation></semantics></math> with <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta=\mathcal{O}(\varepsilon^{\frac{1}{\alpha}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta=\mathcal{O}(\varepsilon^{\frac{1}{\alpha}})</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{*}\!=\mathcal{O}(\varepsilon^{\frac{2}{d_{0}}+\frac{1}{\alpha}})" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.108em">=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{*}\!=\mathcal{O}(\varepsilon^{\frac{2}{d_{0}}+\frac{1}{\alpha}})</annotation></semantics></math> such that <math id="A2.SS2.p1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|\bar{f}-f_{\delta}\right\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>≤</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|\bar{f}-f_{\delta}\right\|_{2}\leq\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math></span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.2" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof"><span id="A2.SS2.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem6" title="Lemma 4.6 (Approximation Error between ℋ̄_{𝑑,𝐿}^𝛼 and ℋ(𝛿)). ‣ 4.1 Approximation for Hölder Class by Piece-wise Constant Function Class ‣ 4 Approximation Error Upper Bound for Hölder Class with Transformers ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.6</span></a></span>.</h6>
<div id="A2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text">Assume <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{x}=d_{y}=d_{0}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mi>y</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{x}=d_{y}=d_{0}</annotation></semantics></math>. Let <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> be positive values to be determined later.</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Suppose we have a grid and cube set:</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}=\left\{0,\delta+\delta^{*},2(\delta+\delta^{*}),\ldots,(M-1)(\delta+\delta^{*})\right\}^{d\times L}~\mathrm{and}~~\left\{\mathcal{S}_{G}\mid G\in\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}\right\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo>{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>and</mi><mo lspace="0.660em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow><mo>}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}=\left\{0,\delta+\delta^{*},2(\delta+\delta^{*}),\ldots,(M-1)(\delta+\delta^{*})\right\}^{d\times L}~\mathrm{and}~~\left\{\mathcal{S}_{G}\mid G\in\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}\right\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.2.1" class="ltx_text">We define the following piece-wise constant function for any <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}\in\bar{\mathcal{H}}_{d,L}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}\in\bar{\mathcal{H}}_{d,L}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="f_{\delta}(X)=\sum\nolimits_{G\in\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}}\bar{f}(G)\cdot\mathds{1}\{X\in\mathcal{S}_{G}\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><msub><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn>𝟙</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\delta}(X)=\sum\nolimits_{G\in\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}}\bar{f}(G)\cdot\mathds{1}\{X\in\mathcal{S}_{G}\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.3.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X,Y\in[0,1]^{d\times L}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X,Y\in[0,1]^{d\times L}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bar{f}=R\circ f\circ R^{-1}\in\bar{\mathcal{H}}_{d,L}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mover accent="true"><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bar{f}=R\circ f\circ R^{-1}\in\bar{\mathcal{H}}_{d,L}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math> w.r.t. <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f\in\mathcal{H}_{d_{0}}^{\alpha}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>∈</mo><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℋ</mi><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f\in\mathcal{H}_{d_{0}}^{\alpha}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex12X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\bar{f}({X})-\bar{f}({Y})\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\bar{f}({X})-\bar{f}({Y})\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\left\|R\circ f\circ R^{-1}({X})-R\circ f\circ R^{-1}({Y})\right\|_{2}=\left\|f\circ R^{-1}({X})-f\circ R^{-1}({Y})\right\|_{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">∘</mo><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\left\|R\circ f\circ R^{-1}({X})-R\circ f\circ R^{-1}({Y})\right\|_{2}=\left\|f\circ R^{-1}({X})-f\circ R^{-1}({Y})\right\|_{2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex12Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex12Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\leq c_{d_{0},K}\left\|R^{-1}({X})-R^{-1}({Y})\right\|_{2}^{\alpha}=c_{1}\left\|{X}-{Y}\right\|_{F}^{\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>R</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\leq c_{d_{0},K}\left\|R^{-1}({X})-R^{-1}({Y})\right\|_{2}^{\alpha}=c_{1}\left\|{X}-{Y}\right\|_{F}^{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p3.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p3.4.1" class="ltx_text">with <math id="A2.SS2.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}\coloneq c_{d_{0},K}=\sqrt{d_{0}}K" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>≔</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}\coloneq c_{d_{0},K}=\sqrt{d_{0}}K</annotation></semantics></math> defined in (<a href="#A2.E18" title="Equation 18 ‣ Lemma B.1 (Smoothness Property of Hölder Class). ‣ B.1 Regularity of the Hölder Class ‣ Appendix B Approximation Error Upper Bound ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">18</span></a>).</span></p>
</div>
<div id="A2.SS2.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.2.1" class="ltx_text">For any <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\mathbb{\mathcal{S}}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\mathbb{\mathcal{S}}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math> and its corresponding grid point <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="G" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>G</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">G</annotation></semantics></math>, the relation <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\|X-{G}\right\|_{F}\leq\sqrt{dL}\delta=\sqrt{d_{0}}\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\|X-{G}\right\|_{F}\leq\sqrt{dL}\delta=\sqrt{d_{0}}\delta</annotation></semantics></math> holds. We get</span></p>
<table id="A2.E19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E19X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E19X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\bar{f}(X)-f_{\delta}(X)\right\|_{F}=\left\|\bar{f}(X)-\bar{f}({G})\right\|_{F}\leq c_{1}\left\|X-{G}\right\|_{F}^{\alpha}\leq c_{1}(\sqrt{d_{0}}\delta)^{\alpha}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>G</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>G</mi></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mi>α</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\bar{f}(X)-f_{\delta}(X)\right\|_{F}=\left\|\bar{f}(X)-\bar{f}({G})\right\|_{F}\leq c_{1}\left\|X-{G}\right\|_{F}^{\alpha}\leq c_{1}(\sqrt{d_{0}}\delta)^{\alpha},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(19)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.3.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, for any <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in[0,1]^{d\times L}\setminus\bigcup_{G\in\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}}\mathcal{S}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo rspace="0.055em">∖</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in[0,1]^{d\times L}\setminus\bigcup_{G\in\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}}\mathcal{S}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E20" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E20X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E20X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\left\|\bar{f}(X)-f_{\delta}(X)\right\|_{F}=\left\|\bar{f}(X)\right\|_{F}\leq\sqrt{dL}K=\sqrt{d_{0}}K." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msqrt><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\left\|\bar{f}(X)-f_{\delta}(X)\right\|_{F}=\left\|\bar{f}(X)\right\|_{F}\leq\sqrt{dL}K=\sqrt{d_{0}}K.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(20)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.4.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, with <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M=\lfloor\frac{1}{\delta+\delta^{*}}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M=\lfloor\frac{1}{\delta+\delta^{*}}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\bigcup_{G}\mathcal{S}_{G}\coloneq\bigcup_{G\in\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}}\mathcal{S}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mi>G</mi></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">≔</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\bigcup_{G}\mathcal{S}_{G}\coloneq\bigcup_{G\in\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}}\mathcal{S}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math>,</span></p>
<table id="A2.E21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.E21.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\begin{aligned} \left\lVert\bar{f}-f_{\delta}\right\rVert_{2}&amp;=\Big(\int_{[0,1]^{d\times L}}\left\|\bar{f}(X)-f_{\delta}(X)\right\|_{F}^{2}\mathrm{d}{X}\Big)^{1/2}\\
&amp;=\Big(\int_{\bigcup_{G}\mathcal{S}_{G}}\left\lVert\bar{f}(X)-f_{\delta}(C_{G})\right\rVert_{F}^{2}\mathrm{d}{X}\Big)^{1/2}+\Big(\int_{[0,1]^{d\times L}\setminus\bigcup_{G}\mathcal{S}_{G}}\left\lVert\bar{f}(X)\right\rVert_{F}^{2}\mathrm{d}{X}\Big)^{1/2}\\
&amp;\leq c_{1}(\sqrt{d_{0}}\delta)^{\alpha}+{(1-M\delta)^{d_{0}/2}\sqrt{d_{0}}K}.\end{aligned}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mtable columnspacing="0pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_right" columnalign="right"><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup></msub><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">⋃</mo><mi>G</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>G</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∫</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></msup><mo>∖</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><msub><mo maxsize="0.700em" minsize="0.700em" stretchy="true">⋃</mo><mi>G</mi></msub></mstyle><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow></mrow></msub><mrow><msubsup><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mi>F</mi><mn>2</mn></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo mathsize="0.700em" rspace="0em">𝑑</mo><mi>X</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>≤</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\!\!\!\!\!\!\!\begin{aligned} \left\lVert\bar{f}-f_{\delta}\right\rVert_{2}&amp;=\Big(\int_{[0,1]^{d\times L}}\left\|\bar{f}(X)-f_{\delta}(X)\right\|_{F}^{2}\mathrm{d}{X}\Big)^{1/2}\\
&amp;=\Big(\int_{\bigcup_{G}\mathcal{S}_{G}}\left\lVert\bar{f}(X)-f_{\delta}(C_{G})\right\rVert_{F}^{2}\mathrm{d}{X}\Big)^{1/2}+\Big(\int_{[0,1]^{d\times L}\setminus\bigcup_{G}\mathcal{S}_{G}}\left\lVert\bar{f}(X)\right\rVert_{F}^{2}\mathrm{d}{X}\Big)^{1/2}\\
&amp;\leq c_{1}(\sqrt{d_{0}}\delta)^{\alpha}+{(1-M\delta)^{d_{0}/2}\sqrt{d_{0}}K}.\end{aligned}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(21)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.5.1" class="ltx_text">For any accuracy <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we first let <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{1}(\sqrt{d_{0}}\delta)^{\alpha}&lt;{\varepsilon}/{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mi>α</mi></msup></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{1}(\sqrt{d_{0}}\delta)^{\alpha}&lt;{\varepsilon}/{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, and it indicates</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A2.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta&lt;\frac{\varepsilon^{1/\alpha}}{(2c_{1})^{1/\alpha}d_{0}^{1/2}}=d_{0}^{-\frac{\alpha+1}{2\alpha}}(2K)^{-\frac{1}{\alpha}}\varepsilon^{\frac{1}{\alpha}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mrow><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msubsup></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mrow><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac></msup></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta&lt;\frac{\varepsilon^{1/\alpha}}{(2c_{1})^{1/\alpha}d_{0}^{1/2}}=d_{0}^{-\frac{\alpha+1}{2\alpha}}(2K)^{-\frac{1}{\alpha}}\varepsilon^{\frac{1}{\alpha}}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.6" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.6.1" class="ltx_text">Denote <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}=(\frac{\varepsilon}{2\sqrt{d_{0}}K})^{2/d_{0}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}=(\frac{\varepsilon}{2\sqrt{d_{0}}K})^{2/d_{0}}</annotation></semantics></math>. If we set a smaller <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> satisfying <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{*}&lt;\frac{(c_{2}-\delta)\delta}{2}&lt;\frac{(c_{2}-\delta)\delta}{1+\delta-c_{2}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{*}&lt;\frac{(c_{2}-\delta)\delta}{2}&lt;\frac{(c_{2}-\delta)\delta}{1+\delta-c_{2}}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></p>
<table id="A2.E22" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">
<tbody>
<tr id="A2.E22X" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle(1-M\delta)^{d_{0}/2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle(1-M\delta)^{d_{0}/2}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.E22X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\sqrt{d_{0}}K\leq\Big(1-\Big(\frac{1}{\delta+\delta^{*}}-1\Big)\delta\Big)^{d_{0}/2}\sqrt{d_{0}}K&lt;\frac{\varepsilon}{2}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mrow><msup><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>/</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msqrt><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></msqrt><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>ε</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\sqrt{d_{0}}K\leq\Big(1-\Big(\frac{1}{\delta+\delta^{*}}-1\Big)\delta\Big)^{d_{0}/2}\sqrt{d_{0}}K&lt;\frac{\varepsilon}{2}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equationgroup ltx_align_right">(22)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.7" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.7.1" class="ltx_text">Therefore, we derive
the error <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\left\lVert\bar{f}-f_{\delta}\right\rVert_{2}&lt;\varepsilon." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mrow><mo>‖</mo><mrow><mover accent="true"><mi>f</mi><mo>¯</mo></mover><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>δ</mi></msub></mrow><mo>‖</mo></mrow><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>ε</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\left\lVert\bar{f}-f_{\delta}\right\rVert_{2}&lt;\varepsilon.</annotation></semantics></math> Equivalently, if we want the right hand of (<a href="#A2.E21" title="Equation 21 ‣ Proof of Lemma . ‣ B.2 Approximation Error Between Hölder Class and Piece-wise Constant Function Class ‣ Appendix B Approximation Error Upper Bound ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">21</span></a>) to be smaller than any accuracy <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\varepsilon&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ε</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\varepsilon&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, we should let</span></p>
<table id="A2.Ex14" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A2.Ex14X"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14X.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14X.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\varepsilon^{\frac{1}{\alpha}}d_{0}^{-\frac{\alpha+1}{2\alpha}}(2K)^{-\frac{1}{\alpha}}=\mathcal{O}(\varepsilon^{\frac{1}{\alpha}})," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mfrac></mrow></msubsup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\varepsilon^{\frac{1}{\alpha}}d_{0}^{-\frac{\alpha+1}{2\alpha}}(2K)^{-\frac{1}{\alpha}}=\mathcal{O}(\varepsilon^{\frac{1}{\alpha}}),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A2.Ex14Xa"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14Xa.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\delta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\delta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A2.Ex14Xa.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle&lt;\frac{(c_{2}-\delta)\delta}{2}=\frac{1}{2}\big(\varepsilon^{\frac{2}{d_{0}}}(2K)^{-\frac{2}{d_{0}}}d_{0}^{-\frac{1}{d_{0}}}-\delta\big)\delta=\mathcal{O}(\varepsilon^{\frac{2}{d_{0}}+\frac{1}{\alpha}})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>ε</mi><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>K</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒪</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msup><mi>ε</mi><mrow><mfrac><mn>2</mn><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>α</mi></mfrac></mrow></msup><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle&lt;\frac{(c_{2}-\delta)\delta}{2}=\frac{1}{2}\big(\varepsilon^{\frac{2}{d_{0}}}(2K)^{-\frac{2}{d_{0}}}d_{0}^{-\frac{1}{d_{0}}}-\delta\big)\delta=\mathcal{O}(\varepsilon^{\frac{2}{d_{0}}+\frac{1}{\alpha}}).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A2.SS2.p4.8" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS2.p4.8.1" class="ltx_text">We clarify that the requirement of <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{2}&gt;\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>c</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>δ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{2}&gt;\delta</annotation></semantics></math> should be satisfied to keep <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta^{*}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta^{*}</annotation></semantics></math> greater than zero. In a sense, this indicates <math id="A2.SS2.p4.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}&gt;2\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}&gt;2\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> and the target function inherently possesses higher input dimension with lower smoothness.
∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A2.SS3" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.3 </span>Approximation for Piece-wise Constant Function Class by Standard Transformers</h3>

<div id="A2.SS3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.SS3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Before starting the proof of components within the standard Transformers, we first demonstrate the novelty and uniqueness of our architecture with related works in this field. See Table <a href="#A2.T3" title="Table 3 ‣ B.3.1 Quantization Module 𝑓_{𝒯⁢1} ‣ B.3 Approximation for Piece-wise Constant Function Class by Standard Transformers ‣ Appendix B Approximation Error Upper Bound ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="A2.SS3.SSS1" class="ltx_subsubsection">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsubsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsubsection">B.3.1 </span>Quantization Module <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathcal{T}1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathcal{T}1}</annotation></semantics></math></h4>

<div id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Lemma <a href="#S4.Thmtheorem7" title="Lemma 4.7 (Quantization Module 𝑓_{𝒯⁢1}). ‣ 4.2 Approximation for Piece-wise Constant Function Class by Standard Transformers ‣ 4 Approximation Error Upper Bound for Hölder Class with Transformers ‣ Approximation Error Upper and Lower Bounds for Hölder Class with Transformers" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.7</span></a></span> (Quantization Module <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathcal{T}1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathcal{T}1}</annotation></semantics></math>; Restatement)<span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span> <span id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Let <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta,\delta^{*}\in(0,1),M=\lfloor\frac{1}{\delta+\delta^{*}}\rfloor" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">⌊</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></mfrac><mo stretchy="false">⌋</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta,\delta^{*}\in(0,1),M=\lfloor\frac{1}{\delta+\delta^{*}}\rfloor</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}=dL" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>d</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}=dL</annotation></semantics></math>. By processing the inputs <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="X\in\bigcup_{G\in\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}}\mathcal{S}_{G}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo rspace="0.111em">∈</mo><mrow><msub><mo>⋃</mo><mrow><mi>G</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub></mrow></msub><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒮</mi><mi>G</mi></msub></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">X\in\bigcup_{G\in\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}}\mathcal{S}_{G}</annotation></semantics></math>, there exists a quantization module <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\mathcal{T}1}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒯</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\mathcal{T}1}</annotation></semantics></math> composed of <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="d_{0}M" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>d</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>M</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">d_{0}M</annotation></semantics></math> feed-forward layers and a positional encoding <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="E=\mathds{1}_{d}\cdot[1,2,\ldots,L]^{\top}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>E</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mn>𝟙</mn><mi>d</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>L</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>⊤</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">E=\mathds{1}_{d}\cdot[1,2,\ldots,L]^{\top}</annotation></semantics></math>, constructing a quantization positional grid <math id="A2.SS3.SSS1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}^{p}=\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}+E" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mi>p</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒢</mi><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><msup><mi>δ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>E</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}^{p}=\mathcal{G}_{\delta,\delta^{*}}+E</annotation></semantics></math>.</span></p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.T3" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A2.T3.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 3</span>: </span><span id="A2.T3.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Novelty and uniqueness in our constructions of Transformers.</span></figcaption>
<table id="A2.T3.5" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_align_middle">
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
